{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And she bore.</b> For Moses said, \"Now Zipporah is the Cushite woman\" that he mentioned. And as for what is written in Chronicles, do not believe it. I tell you as a general principle: any book not written by prophets or by sages from received tradition is not to be relied upon — all the more so if it contains matters that contradict sound reason. Such is the book of Zerubbabel, and also the book of Eldad the Danite, and what resembles them."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The quotation \"Now Zipporah is the Cushite woman\" appears to paraphrase Numbers 12:1, Ibn Ezra's cross-reference for identifying Zipporah with the Cushite woman; the Hebrew reads slightly elliptically and is rendered as presented."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:09.583524931Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}